# Auth Types — quarantined, not part of the CI sweep

Four `auth` block variants, each against an [httpbin.org](https://httpbin.org) endpoint built specifically to validate that auth scheme. **This file lives outside the paths `.github/workflows/validate-void.yml` runs** because, under `@voiden/runner@2.3.0-beta.19`, three of its four sections currently fail for real (not an assertion nuance — the underlying HTTP request itself comes back `401`), which would otherwise make every push/PR red for a reason unrelated to whatever's actually being changed. See `KNOWN-ISSUES.md` #1 and #2 for the full diagnosis.

Every assertion below is left **enabled** on purpose (unlike the disabled-with-a-note pattern used elsewhere in this repo) — this file is meant to be run directly, on demand, to check whether a fix has landed:

```
voiden-runner run "Automated Tests/Known Broken (Beta)/Auth Types.void" --profile --no-session
```

A section going green here is the signal to move this file back into `Automated Tests/` and add it back into the CI paths.

