Unlike bearer/basic/digest, this section's underlying request doesn't 401 (httpbin's plain `/get` accepts anything), so it stays green at the request level even though the assertion above fails — that inconsistency is itself part of `KNOWN-ISSUES.md` #0.

```void
---
type: request-separator
attrs:
  uid: "72e4c2f9-ae69-446a-a33e-20d319b32a5c"
  colorIndex: 3
  label: "Digest Auth"
---
```

The trickiest of the four — digest auth is a real challenge/response round trip (an initial 401 with a `WWW-Authenticate` challenge, then a re-request with a computed digest). A passing section here proves that whole flow works, not just that credentials were attached somewhere. Broken on both the stable and beta channels (see `KNOWN-ISSUES.md` #2) — this one's independent of the bearer/basic/apiKey regression above.

